<!-- <html>/<body> are ignored - only <body>'s children are copied into the page. -->
<!--
    Top protective-marking bar placeholder (issue #175).

    Bind this file to the "webhelp.fragment.before.body" placeholder, which is
    included at the start of <body> on ALL four generated page types (main
    /tiles, topic, search results, index terms). The element below is
    deliberately EMPTY: xslt/inc/customProtection.xsl matches it in
    `copy_template` mode and either fills it with the marking text or drops it
    entirely, according to the webhelp.show.protection / webhelp.protection.text
    scenario parameters.

    Do not put the marking text here. Literal text in this file would be part
    of the template, and on a one-way air-gapped gateway a template edit costs
    a full re-transfer; a scenario parameter costs nothing.

    The <html>/<body> wrapper is not decoration: Oxygen's includeCustomHTMLContent
    copies only <body>'s children when it finds that wrapper, and copies the WHOLE
    document - these comments included - when it does not.
-->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <body>
        <header class="wh_header_protection"/>
    </body>
</html>
